              "id": "CVE-2018-18064",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2018-18064"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2018-18064?s=ubuntu&n=cairo&ns=ubuntu&t=deb&osn=ubuntu&osv=24.04&vr=%3E%3D0",
              "help": {
                "text": "cairo through 1.15.14 has an out-of-bounds stack-memory write during processing of a crafted document by WebKitGTK+ because of the interaction between cairo-rectangular-scan-converter.c (the generate and render_rows functions) and cairo-image-compositor.c (the _cairo_image_spans_and_zero function).\n",
                "markdown": "> cairo through 1.15.14 has an out-of-bounds stack-memory write during processing of a crafted document by WebKitGTK+ because of the interaction between cairo-rectangular-scan-converter.c (the generate and render_rows functions) and cairo-image-compositor.c (the _cairo_image_spans_and_zero function).\n\n|                                                                                                                                                                    |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:deb/ubuntu/cairo@1.18.0-3build1?os_distro=noble&os_name=ubuntu&os_version=24.04  |\n|Affected range                                                                 >=0                                                                                  |\n|Fixed version                                                                  not fixed                                                                            |\n|[[CVSS Score 6.5] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H]]                                                                                       |\n"
