              "help": {
                "text": "The team has identified a critical vulnerability in the http server of the most recent version of Node, where malformed headers can lead to HTTP request smuggling. Specifically, if a space is placed before a content-length header, it is not interpreted correctly, enabling attackers to smuggle in a second request within the body of the first.\n",
                "markdown": "> The team has identified a critical vulnerability in the http server of the most recent version of Node, where malformed headers can lead to HTTP request smuggling. Specifically, if a space is placed before a content-length header, it is not interpreted correctly, enabling attackers to smuggle in a second request within the body of the first.\n\n|                                                                                                            |\n|Package         pkg:deb/ubuntu/nodejs@22.23.2-1nodesource1?os_distro=noble&os_name=ubuntu&os_version=24.04  |\n|Affected range  >=0                                                                                         |\n|Fixed version   not fixed                                                                                   |\n"
