            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-18508",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-18508"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-18508?s=ubuntu&n=tar&ns=ubuntu&t=deb&osn=ubuntu&osv=24.04&vr=%3E%3D0",
              "help": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in GNU tar. When extracting an archive with the --one-top-level option, hardlink targets are not confined to the designated top-level directory and may resolve relative to the extraction working directory. A crafted archive can create hardlinks that escape the intended boundary and, when combined with a preexisting symbolic link under the working directory, may allow writing outside that boundary during a single extraction.\n",
                "markdown": "> A flaw was found in GNU tar. When extracting an archive with the --one-top-level option, hardlink targets are not confined to the designated top-level directory and may resolve relative to the extraction working directory. A crafted archive can create hardlinks that escape the intended boundary and, when combined with a preexisting symbolic link under the working directory, may allow writing outside that boundary during a single extraction.\n\n|                                                                                                           |\n|Package         pkg:deb/ubuntu/tar@1.35%2Bdfsg-3ubuntu0.4?os_distro=noble&os_name=ubuntu&os_version=24.04  |\n|Affected range  >=0                                                                                        |\n|Fixed version   not fixed                                                                                  |\n"
