            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-9496",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-9496: Inefficient Regular Expression Complexity"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-9496?s=github&n=pacote&t=npm&vr=%3E%3D11.2.7%2C%3C21.5.1",
              "help": {
                "text": "Versions of the package pacote from 11.2.7 are vulnerable to Denial of Service (DoS) via the addGitSha function. An attacker can exploit this vulnerability by supplying a specially crafted spec.rawSpec value that triggers the function’s regex replacement and string-manipulation logic, causing excessive CPU consumption and potentially stalling or crashing the process.\n",
                "markdown": "> Versions of the package pacote from 11.2.7 are vulnerable to Denial of Service (DoS) via the addGitSha function. An attacker can exploit this vulnerability by supplying a specially crafted spec.rawSpec value that triggers the function’s regex replacement and string-manipulation logic, causing excessive CPU consumption and potentially stalling or crashing the process.\n\n|                                                                                                                             |\n|Package                                                                                               pkg:npm/pacote@20.0.1  |\n|Affected range                                                                                        >=11.2.7,<21.5.1       |\n|Fixed version                                                                                         21.5.1                 |\n|[[CVSS Score 7.7] [CVSS Vector CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:P]]                         |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
